    "summary": "L8 global integration / functional access: 4 [V] / 1 [O]. A global metastable RESONANT HUB integrates the L1-L7 modules. (G1) the gate SELECTS one module, the hub resonance-LOCKS to its concept (margin>0), and a NON-SOURCE module recovers that concept from the BROADCAST alone where a no-hub control is at chance -- information becomes globally available. (G2) moving the gate FLEXIBLY ROUTES any module's content to the whole system; a fixed gate reaches only its one module -- routing is reconfigurable, not hard-wired. (G3) the FUNCTIONAL PCI-analog (integration x differentiation of the modules' response to a hub kick: how far the perturbation SPREADS times how DISTINCT the modules stay) is HIGH engaged but LOW both isolated (no integration, I=0) and over-driven (no differentiation, D->0): access peaks at the metastable edge -- the inherited Gap-4 inverted-U, the NUMBER R=0.39 not transferred. (G4) the honest inherited limit: the hub must route WITHIN the modules' latch band -- a non-empty within-band regime where routing holds [V], with too-fast switching collapsing integration [O] (the L7 operating-band limit, now concrete for the global hub). FIREWALL: 'access' is broadcast availability ONLY; no felt experience is claimed in any regime. new_tuned_constants = 0."
